<function-requirements>

<input>
project name: w3m
function signature: Str Strnew_m_charp(const char *, void)
</input>

<description>
The function `Strnew_m_charp` is a variadic function that concatenates a variable number of C-style strings into a single `Str` object. It takes a variable number of `const char *` arguments, terminated by a `NULL` pointer. The function initializes a new `Str` object and appends each string argument to it.
</description>

<requirements>
<requirement>
The last argument to `Strnew_m_charp` must be a `NULL` pointer. This is because the function uses a `NULL` pointer to determine the end of the variable argument list.
</requirement>
<requirement>
Each argument must be a null-terminated string. The function uses `strlen` to determine the length of each string, so a missing null terminator will result in a buffer over-read.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `GC_INIT()` function must be called before calling `Strnew_m_charp`. This is because the `Str` object and its internal buffer are allocated using the Boehm garbage collector, and `GC_INIT()` is required to initialize the garbage collector.
</requirement>
</requirements>

</function-requirements>

